OPERATOR DECISION (2026-08-07): CLEAN BREAK — no alias.

`--force-close` is renamed to `--force` on transition outright. No compatibility alias ships. Rationale matches the epic-2f79 precedent for retiring `reconcile`: a stale caller should fail loudly with an unknown-flag error rather than silently continuing to work, and an alias would keep both spellings alive in help, docs and muscle memory indefinitely.

Implementation implications:
- every in-repo call site and doc reference migrates in the SAME change (search for the string, not just the symbol — CLI flags appear in docs, tests, skills and prompt text);
- argparse must reject `--force-close` with a clear error naming the new spelling, NOT silently abbreviation-match it. Note 424f is setting `allow_abbrev=False` for exactly this class of hazard;
- CHANGELOG entry required, since this is user-visible and breaking.
